{
  "title": "Cape Historical Data Repository",
  "upload_type": "dataset",
  "version": "1.0",
  "license": "cc-by-4.0",
  "description": "<p>Five collections of records on the Cape Colony, 1650–1850, released by LEAP (Laboratory for the Economics of Africa's Past), Stellenbosch University: cleaned tables of the opgaaf tax censuses (1660–1844, ten districts; 325,628 tax units), the 1834 slave emancipation records (36,417 records) and the South African Families genealogies (213,953 people born up to 1870 and 153,568 marriages), in CSV and Parquet; and the transcription XML of the Orphan Chamber probate inventories (MOOC8; 5,953 documents, 1673–1844) and estate auction rolls (MOOC10; 3,266 auctions, 1691–1834). Every file and column is described in the collections' READMEs and in datapackage.json.</p><p>Users must cite the paper(s) for each collection they use, listed in the README and below, and this release.</p>",
